-- #b and the same bytes from the next offset, or nil), so every definition on List Word reads it unchanged; a
-- copy shares the bytes (refcount). w-file-read gives a file as one V_TEXT: n bytes and one cell, where the list
-- built at once was n cons cells (64 bytes each) and n word cells (56 bytes each), 120n bytes held before any
-- of it was read; reading it now holds the cells of the part being read and no more. The writers take a text
-- rest whole (drv_text_tail). Every page of the site is byte-identical under the old and new machine.
-- src/net.c (2026-11-18, /chat in compiled code): a text crosses into compiled code as its bytes. Forcing
